# P1: created, never freed or transferred -> leak (info) at the create site
object-leak 8
# P2: freed in the finally -> no leak
!object-leak 14
# P3: ownership returned via Result -> no leak
!object-leak 19
# P4: passed to a call (escape) -> no leak
!object-leak 24
# B9 -- exit/break inside a try..FINALLY run the finally before leaving, so the
# object IS freed on the divert path. Before exit diverted at all this could not
# be got wrong; making it divert is what put the question on the table.
# P5: guard clause inside try..finally -> no leak
!object-leak 33
# P6: break out of a loop, from inside a try..finally -> no leak
!object-leak 47
# P7 CONTROL: the exit is OUTSIDE the try, so nothing frees it -> leak
object-leak 61
